moveOne subtracts one from its first variable and adds one to its second. -= subtracts and stores. Passing count to both parameters conflicts with exclusive access; two different variables would be valid. This complete local compiler example is intentionally rejected. It is not a runtime exercise; do not repair it with unsafe access.
```swift
func moveOne(_ source: inout Int, to destination: inout Int) {
    source -= 1
    destination += 1
}
func demonstrateConflict() {
    var count = 5
    moveOne(&count, to: &count)
}
demonstrateConflict()
```
